    "result_text": "Done. The build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: reject with **429** once 100+ owners have already been created today (by `registrationDate`).\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added the behaviour as **small new units** rather than growing any existing class/method (no existing function was edited \u2014 only one line-block added to the YAML wiring):\n\n- **`RequireDailyLimit`** \u2014 a new guard function (one method) that counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and throws when `>= 100`. Modeled on the existing `RequireCityCapacity`.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** \u2014 new checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause and is routed by escalation).\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 new handler responding `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`, mirroring the existing capacity handler's `ProblemDetails` pattern.\n- **`...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** \u2014 new escalation mapping.\n- Wired `dailyLimit` as the first step in `owners.POST.yml` (a read-only precheck, before the write pipeline).\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` and the full suite are green.",
